      "writtenOn": "2023-04-25T05:59:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This doesn\u0027t really address my previous comment. The problem is that the caller must not forget to call this, which is very difficult to guarantee.\n\nCan you build it in such a way that it\u0027s impossible to get it wrong from the caller\u0027s point of view ? A simple way to do this is to offer as the only way to get the data a method that returns a snapshot and resets the time. Then it\u0027s not possible to forget calling reset.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 109,
        "startChar": 20,
        "endLine": 109,
        "endChar": 38
      },
      "revId": "785f5b8eeaf9c0214e28423ce667ac4243855019",
